{{ang-decl-noun-o-f|treow|alt1=trēow}}

=====Descendants=====
*English: [[truce]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*trewą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*drew-o-}}, a suffixed variant of {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*drew-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*deru-||solid, steadfast}}, whence probably also {{etyl|ine-pro|-}} noun for "tree" {{m|ine-pro|*dóru}}. Germanic cognates include {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|trē}}, {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|treo}}, {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|tré}} ({{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|træ}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍄𐍂𐌹𐌿}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|δόρυ||wood, spear}}, {{m|grc|δρῦς||tree, oak}}, {{etyl|cu|-}} {{m|cu|дрѣво|sc=Cyrs}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|де́рево}}), {{etyl|sga|-}} {{m|sga|daur}} ({{etyl|cy|-}} {{m|cy|derwen||oak}}).

====Noun====
{{ang-noun|n|head=trēow}}

# [[tree]]

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-n|treow|alt1=trēow}}

=====Descendants=====
* English: {{l|en|tree}}

